|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_f_f_

    !! For functions $f$ with what kind of
    !! signature does the composition
    !! $$
    !! f \circ f
    !! $$
    !! make sense?
    What constraints does the composition
    $$
    f \circ f
    $$
    impose on the signature of $f$?

    |> Solution

        A signature of the form 
        $$
        f : [\tA] \ra [\tA]
        $$
        is necessary and sufficient.
        Formally, the general composition

        $$
        f \circ g
        $$

        requires signatures of the form

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        f : [\B] \ra [\C] \\
        \up{1.6}g : [\A] \ra [\B]
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        for some units A, B, C, as per >>table_1_1.
        If $g = f$
        this implies $\A = \B$ because both are the inputs
        of $f = g$, as well as $\B = \C$ because both are
        the outputs of $f = g$, collapsing A, B, C to a
        single unit $\A = \B = \C = \A$.


        !!     the composition

        !!     $$
        !!     f\circ g
        !!     $$

        !!     is well-formed if and ony if $[\tD] = [\tA]$. 
        !!     (Cf. [Table 1.1](>>table_1_1).)
        !!     In our case $g = f$ so we additionally have

        !!     $$
        !!     \begin{gathered}
        !!     !! found mathjax bug that requires this \up{0}:
        !!     \up{0}[\tC] = [\tA] \\
        !!     \up{1.6}[\tD] = [\tB]
        !!     \end{gathered}
        !!     $$

        !!     to start with, which, together with 
        !!     $[\tD] = [\tA]$, collapses the signature of $f$
        !!     to “$[\tA] \ra [\tA]$”.

        !! |> SolutionNote
        !!     Formally,
        !!     two functions $f$, $g$ of general signature

        !!     $$
        !!     \begin{gathered}
        !!     f : [\tA] \ra [\tB] \\
        !!     \up{1.6}g : [\tC] \ra [\tD]
        !!     \end{gathered}
        !!     $$

        !!     the composition

        !!     $$
        !!     f\circ g
        !!     $$

        !!     is well-formed if and ony if $[\tD] = [\tA]$. 
        !!     (Cf. [Table 1.1](>>table_1_1).)
        !!     In our case $g = f$ so we additionally have

        !!     $$
        !!     \begin{gathered}
        !!     !! found mathjax bug that requires this \up{0}:
        !!     \up{0}[\tC] = [\tA] \\
        !!     \up{1.6}[\tD] = [\tB]
        !!     \end{gathered}
        !!     $$

        !!     to start with, which, together with 
        !!     $[\tD] = [\tA]$, collapses the signature of $f$
        !!     to “$[\tA] \ra [\tA]$”.
